messages.content:
You are working on an e-commerce website and have noticed that the product image carousel is not fully accessible. Upon inspection, you find that the carousel is missing a few key accessibility features: the images do not have alternative text, the carousel lacks keyboard navigation support, and the images are not wrapped in a <figure> tag for better semantic meaning. Your task is to fix these issues in the carousel. Here is the starter markup you will be working with:
<div class='carousel'>
  <img src='product1.jpg'>
  <img src='product2.jpg'>
  <img src='product3.jpg'>
</div>
<style>
.carousel img {
  width: 100%;
  display: none;
}
.carousel img:first-child {
  display: block;
}
</style>
